<%# Faithful port of the legacy SPA `Hujah/card_header.js`: avatar + full_name + @handle,
    plus a menu (native <details>, no JS needed). Optional `parent:` local
    renders the "Response to ..." parent stub (port of card_parent.js).

    HOOJAH 2026 (redesign Phase 1, Task 1.3) — mockup ~217-224. Two changes from the
    Slice 9 shape:

    - The avatar is now the gradient-initials TILE (`variant: :tile`, `size: :row` —
      40px, docs/design-system/components/hujah/HujahHeader.prompt.md's byline box),
      not the round photo. The name drops the Slice-9 `text-primary` — the mockup's
      byline name is `font-weight:700` in `var(--ink)`, indigo is no longer the
      identity colour here — and `@handle · date` moves from `text-sm text-grey` to
      the 2026 caption pairing `text-xs text-ink-2` used everywhere else this shape
      appears (`hujahs/show`'s own byline, `debates/_debate_card`'s label). There is no
      verified badge: this product has no `User#verified?` concept, so none is added.
    - The two separate triggers Slice 9 left here — a bare `share-2` icon for
      `_share_menu`'s own `<details>`, no flag control at all — collapse into ONE
      `more-vertical` trigger (mockup: a single circle-dots glyph, not two icons). The
      panel underneath is both existing menus' content unchanged — the six share intent
      links plus the native-share button (still carrying `_share_menu`'s
      `data-controller="share"` and its three `data-share-*-value` attributes, unmoved,
      because `spec/system/share_spec.rb` selects on them) and the flag dialog trigger
      (`hujahs/_flag_dialog`, its own `data-controller="dialog"` also unmoved) — so
      neither flow's HTML contract changes, only their shared entry point. There was no
      flag control on the feed card before this task; the show page's separate "More
      actions" menu (which does the same share+flag consolidation, just under a
      `more-horizontal` glyph) is untouched — it renders its own header, not this
      partial, and its system specs (`share_spec`, `flag_spec`) exercise it directly.

    Both avatars go through `ui/_avatar` — the tile (`row`, 40px) for the byline, 32px
    (`sm`) for the parent stub, which are the design system's own boxes for those two
    slots. That is not only tidiness: `image_tag user.photo` RAISES when `photo` is
    blank, and `:photo` is user-editable while `assign_random_photo` only backfills on
    create. This partial renders inside every feed card, so one photoless author 500s
    the whole feed. Pass the box through `size:`, never a `w-*` in `class:` — those
    compete rather than override, and the bundle's order decides (see the partial's own
    header).

    The stub's `shadow-sm` stays. It is the only `shadow-sm` in the app and it is NOT
    the card shadow: this strip sits above the byline inside a card that already has
    `shadow`, and promoting it to a full `shadow` would read as a second card edge —
    which is precisely what ui/_divider's header says internal sections must not grow. %>
<% if local_assigns[:parent].present? %>
  <%= link_to hujah_path(parent.slug), class: "block no-underline" do %>
    <div class="shadow-sm border-b border-light-grey px-4 py-1 flex items-center">
      <%= render "ui/avatar", user: parent.user, size: :sm, class: "mr-2" %>
      <div class="flex flex-col min-w-0">
        <small class="text-sm text-grey">
          Response to <span class="text-primary"><%= parent.user.full_name %></span>'s hoojah
        </small>
        <div class="text-grey text-sm truncate max-w-[350px]"><%= strip_tags(parent.body) %></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  <% end %>
<% end %>

<div class="px-4 pt-3 pb-0 flex justify-between items-center">
  <div class="flex items-center min-w-0">
    <%= link_to "#", class: "shrink-0" do %>
      <%= render "ui/avatar", user: hujah.user, variant: :tile, size: :row, class: "mr-3" %>
    <% end %>
    <div class="flex flex-col min-w-0">
      <%= link_to hujah.user.full_name, "#", class: "text-ink font-bold no-underline truncate" %>
      <small class="text-xs text-ink-2">
        @<%= hujah.user.username %>
        <span class="mx-1">·</span>
        <%# `data-local="time-ago"` is local_time's hook — the compact "%b %-d" here is
            the server-rendered fallback the design system specifies, not a placeholder. %>
        <time datetime="<%= hujah.created_at.iso8601 %>" data-local="time-ago"><%= hujah.created_at.strftime("%b %-d") %></time>
      </small>
    </div>
  </div>

  <%= render "hujahs/card_menu", hujah: hujah %>
</div>
